{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/745840-revamping-werewolf-the-apocalypse-what-would-you-do","id":745840,"title":"Revamping Werewolf: the Apocalypse - What would you do?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-31T22:47:47-07:00","id":745840,"title":"Revamping Werewolf: the Apocalypse - What would you do?","content":"WtA has, over the years, had some legitimate criticism leveled at it. Like a lot of cWoD games it has the flaws of a 90's game before research became easily available. There are elements, which in this day and age, looks a little close-minded. However, this thread isn't exactly about that. If you had creative control over the future of WtA, what would you do? What would you fix, changes or add to the line? This assumes that it is a reboot of the line, updated for the modern age. How would you change the tribes. Would you change the breeds? Does Metis serve a purpose enough to keep, or should it have a name change? Should the Garou language be expanded on (much like the First Tongue of WtF). Would you change the mechanics? And in which way?<br /> <br /> For me, there is a lot I would change. I was attached to Werewolf since it was my first WoD game. (A Bastet lore-keeper of sorts), but looking back at it and through my copy of W20, it seems to have aged. These days I have preferred the Forsaken, but with the possibility of a Werewolf game being made by our new Overlords, I'm looking back at my old WtA books. Since Apocalypse will, most likely, the world that is used for the media projects, I'm catching up on Apocalypse, and since we will most likely get an updated world, I'm wondering what people would want. <br /> <br /> I haven't gotten through and digested all of W20, but I'm sure thoughts will come to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T23:02:29-07:00","id":745899,"title":"","content":"I feel mechanics are the only major problem. I feel changing the lore will kill it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T23:09:43-07:00","id":745936,"title":"","content":"If I may ask, why? Do you not feel the criticism to the setting has any merit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T23:37:35-07:00","id":745955,"title":"","content":"Let the Ahadi or Hengeyokai or some other group that lets you play multibreed groups in Europe and the Americas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T01:36:22-07:00","id":746082,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/745840-revamping-werewolf-the-apocalypse-what-would-you-do#post745840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are elements, which in this day and age, looks a little close-minded.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/745840-revamping-werewolf-the-apocalypse-what-would-you-do?p=745936#post745936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I may ask, why? Do you not feel the criticism to the setting has any merit?</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh oh. Is this gonna turn into that damned 'Alternatives to Vampires or a &quot;Post-Gehenna&quot; setting' thread? I have little interest in excoriating the game I love to make it more palatable to those who get offended by their gaming books...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 11-01-2015, 03:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T01:51:31-07:00","id":746119,"title":"","content":"If I could revamp Werewolf, I'd try to make the combat run a bit smoother. Precisely how I'd do that, I'm not sure, but that's why I'm not a game designer or prolific homebrewer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1069-archmage-joda","name":"Archmage Joda","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T01:53:09-08:00","id":746211,"title":"","content":"Werewolf is an amazing game with depths that are not obvious at first. The social and the spiritual depth of the setting are deeply engrossing and intriguing. The errors of research are minor things in the grand scale, and they're easy to adapt or ignore, especially with all the cultural, historical and biological references we have available these days. I wouldn't want to make a new and different Werewolf, because this one is great.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't mind some tribe books being written all over again, though, since some of them had had a huge disservice done to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T02:15:24-08:00","id":746228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/745840-revamping-werewolf-the-apocalypse-what-would-you-do?p=746082#post746082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Uh oh. Is this gonna turn into that damned 'Alternatives to Vampires or a &quot;Post-Gehenna&quot; setting' thread? I have little interest in excoriating the game I love to make it more palatable to those who get offended by their gaming books...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's quite a jump for conclusion to what I was saying. Updating a setting means taking a hard look at everything written. There has been over a decade of things to look back and see what worked and what did not. Wondering why someone thinks something says nothing else. I'd appreciate you not jumping to conclusions and being backhanded about it while you are at it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T03:36:02-08:00","id":746290,"title":"","content":"Things I would change:<br /> <br /> Mechanics (beyond just cleaning up the cWOD system in general) -<br /> <br /> 1) Gifts. The current Gift structure is extremely clunky. While I don't want it moved to something like Disciplines, I think there are much better ways to express their diversity that can be much easier on bookkeeping, and also help some of the weirder mechanic-to-fluff disconnects go away.<br /> <br /> 2) Rites. While the Rites themselves are rarely a problem, getting them is a pain. A lot of the rites are highly narrative/plot driven in function, but eat up the same amount of resources (freebies or time) as the ones that actually matter to vital mechanics. The simple fix for this is just to divide them up that way explicitly. Have some rites that anyone that meets the general requirements is assumed to know, or can try without a massive penalty, and other rights that need to be formally taught.<br /> <br /> 3) Dump the rather inane value disparity in the starting Rage/Gnosis/Willpower assignments. I've posted my personal fix for this in the past. Possibly also have each Breed have a weakness.<br /> <br /> 4) Totem creation rules. Large lists of Totems are nice, but I see so few of them get used because the pricing on others is just too good, and bans can make some Totems useless no matter how flavorful, while others are easy to turn into passes just by living in specific places. Just have the tools to make the Totem you want, that can also be adjusted more easily to the ST's setting (aka following a Totem that demands you protect its physical relatives is worth more if the game is set where they are under significant threat, than if the game is set somewhere those animals don't even exist.<br /> <br /> 5) Tribal Bans over Tribal Weaknesses/Background Restrictions (unless they're part of the Ban); though keep the discouraged Backgrounds from W20.<br /> <br /> 6) Scrap the current Renown award structure, so Renown can actually be a better gauge of how Renowned your werewolves are. Have Renown awarded at Moots based on retelling the pack's deeds (with plenty of boasting and embellishments); which avoids annoying bookkeeping and gives you actual things to use as what other Garou have heard about your characters.<br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> Setting/Lore -<br /> <br /> 1) I don't need the Garou Tongue to be an invented language like Forsaken, but lets change it to something that makes sense as a linguistic whole. Words borrowed from dozens of languages willy-nilly gets really silly.<br /> <br /> 2) Something else I've gone on at length about before: Fix the Red Talons to give them something to do besides hate humans more than everyone else. My personal favored approach is to have them be the &quot;Wyld&quot; Garou to the GW's &quot;Weaver&quot; Garou. The Red Talons aren't just the big bad wolves lurking in the woods, but they're actively trying to break humanity's dominance over nature by bringing back more Wyld and letting it lose on the world.<br /> <br /> 3) More alternatives to the Garou Nation, and less Tribal exclusivity to those groups. The Garou Nation can still be dominant in the setting thanks to European colonialism (much like the Camarilla), but have a Pure Ones Alliance in the Americans that includes more than just the Uktena and Wendigo, but also the Red Talons, Bone Gnawers, and an much longer in the New World strain of the Silver Fangs<br /> <br /> 4) Give the kin more to do than be breeding stock. I'm not looking to change the overall power dynamic, but give the kin more of a place in the setting besides &quot;family you care about/people you bone.&quot; The current situation is kind of silly with the kin being far too numerous, and necessary, for the Garou to really use large scale violence to keep them in line, but they have no real incentive to become third class citizens to the Garou when they could just go off and live their own lives. It doesn't have to be much - it doesn't even have to be mechanical - just something that clearly says, &quot;being a kin that's active with the Garou provides benefits other options don't.&quot; <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T04:37:11-08:00","id":746372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/745840-revamping-werewolf-the-apocalypse-what-would-you-do?p=746290#post746290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 6) Scrap the current Renown award structure, so Renown can actually be a better gauge of how Renowned your werewolves are. Have Renown awarded at Moots based on retelling the pack's deeds (with plenty of boasting and embellishments); which avoids annoying bookkeeping and gives you actual things to use as what other Garou have heard about your characters.<br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> 4) Give the kin more to do than be breeding stock. I'm not looking to change the overall power dynamic, but give the kin more of a place in the setting besides &quot;family you care about/people you bone.&quot; The current situation is kind of silly with the kin being far too numerous, and necessary, for the Garou to really use large scale violence to keep them in line, but they have no real incentive to become third class citizens to the Garou when they could just go off and live their own lives. It doesn't have to be much - it doesn't even have to be mechanical - just something that clearly says, &quot;being a kin that's active with the Garou provides benefits other options don't.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, to 6, that is how it actually goes in the books. Galliards tell tales and renown -should- mean what is known about the character. Sadly, it isn't always done like that, and renown becomes just dots.<br /> <br /> As for Kinfolk, their job is to be the eyes and ears of the nation among humans. They do all the jobs most garou cannot do, and report to garou any dangers they encounter. Again, it is more the way kinfolk are treated and played that creates the problem, not how they are in books.<br /> <br /> My own suggestions;<br /> <br /> -Clarify minor things. Such as if garou revert to breed form while asleep.<br /> <br /> - Rename the metis breed, 'metis' is a tribe of native americans, and I think it being used in the context it is in WtA is kind of.. yeah.<br /> <br /> -Rename Thrall of the Wyrm to something more subtler. Rage is of the Wyrm is an aspect of the setting I am not very fond of, and aside from that, I feel the name alone discourages people from playing their characters once they thrall. Especially the metis.<br /> <br /> -Have more factions outside of the Nation. Currently, it is simply Nation, BSDs and the ronin. I would like there being a faction that wants to cure their werewolf nature, few cults that don't share Gaian beliefs, etc. Basically, just muddle the waters. I especially want the cure seeking faction, because WtA doesn't really have that aspect of werewolf mythos, outside the Reculant garou nature and some ronin.<br /> <br /> -This sounds strange, but being an online gamer, this has popped up a lot. Fix how purebreed affects breeding to reflect the setting. Currently, breeding gives you a bonus in breeding garou. Yet, the most numerous tribes lack breeding all together. Someone even figured out that purebreed -weakening- the chances of breeding true would make more sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T05:05:56-08:00","id":746389,"title":"","content":"First I don't care for Forsaken, my personal opinion. As for setting changes: <br /> 1. The universal ban of silver is plenty powerful, but options are the key. Many people like the Yava of the Bastet I would have no problem with each tribe having 2-3 secrets that act as tribal bans. <br /> 2. Certain tribes are poorly defined and while some of have been corrected by various supplements others remain two dimensional. These tribes need a bit of an overhaul: Bone Gnawers the idea of omega wolves let alone a tribe needs to die. I have no issue with the Gnawers being misfits, or having wealth and pure breed restrictions but to have an entire tribe that actually are the largest and most likely to be ignored based on totem affiliation is problematic.<br /> 2a. The Children of Gaia need a fixed purpose and the entire privileged upper middle class whining that seems inherit to the tribe needs to die in a fire during a tornado.<br /> 2b. Silent Striders cursed by a vampire driven from a portion of their territory the Striders as a tribe need a home. I don't mind the wandering travelers as a character concept, but an entire tribe is a bit much. <br /> 2c. Red Talons I don't mind the tribe hating humans, I don't mind them even longing for the death of a majority of the species I have an issue that as written they are murderhobos. A better write up along the lines of the all lupus tribe cares only for wolves and has no love of humanity and will do everything in their power to protect their dwindling kin.<br /> 3. The emphasis on Pentex as the entire sum of the Wyrm's war effort. This is not the case but many players seem to think it is when I use Pentex I do so sparingly a branch here or there.<br /> 4. The Black Spiral Dancers- look I understand the greatest foe is the mirror image of the characters and all but the BSD as written up to W20 made little to no sense go back and read the original histories. I want the Black Spiral to be cunning the hidden knife at the throat of the Garou Nation the golden cub that is actually the traitor. The revered elder who secretly dines on children and abuses his wife. The Black Spiral in other words should be from all tribes and hidden among them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T10:14:41-08:00","id":746968,"title":"","content":"It's less about stuff in the corebook, but how certain things were developed. Some things that were developed are good and works for me. Some things really don't add value, but they don't distract either. Some things go against what I want to do in the game, and I ignore them and do my own thing. No matter how a game develops, that is always going to be true. However, I would definitely present some of this information differently than how the game does it.<br /> <br /> 1) The game's materials should always be a toolkit that allows the ST to run the game he wants to run. Too often in White Wolf history, supplements present someone's campaign he thinks is cool and wants to force down everyone else's throat as metaplot. Revised was particularly bad that way. The 20th Edition books are much better and in the spirit of early 2nd Edition.<br /> <br /> 2) Too often the setting strays far away from what I think are werewolves. Instead of being based on popular culture and folklore, Garou seem to be their own fantasy race. While you can't fault players from taking things and running with it, I think those traditional elements should be emphasized in official products. In theory, the game already has concepts and mechanics to do this (Lost Cubs, Lunatics, Ronin, certain Merits and Flaws, the Curse, certain Fetishes), but in practice it does not come off that way. Instead of being prominent elements the setting has to deal with, they are things mostly ignored in my experience.<br /> <br /> 3) A major problem is overuse of Crinos form. Whenever I see some Crinos holding pistols, wearing specialized made clothing, or other things that make it &quot;normal&quot; I want to puke. It doesn't look &quot;cool&quot; to me, I think it looks lame (I may be in the minority here). It makes the Garou much more like creatures that should be in a fantasy game than in a horror game. In my game, I hold that Crinos don't have precision grip or even a true opposable thumb. People can use Homid or Glabro if they want to do that. I'd like to have the game utilize the other forms much more.<br /> <br /> 4) The game needs expanded antagonists. Industrial pollution fomori certainly have their place, but it should be as one kind of antagonist. I use a lot of Lovecraftian concepts to introduce new kinds of fomori, monsters, and banes. It does a good job of really making things horrofic, and introduces a lot of mystery. The game needs multiple kinds of &quot;large target&quot; groups like Pentex - large scale Wyrm cults, big evil books that grant mortals infernalist magics that disturb the earth, deep umbral horrors with their own conspiracies, etc.<br /> <br /> 5) Introduce more antagonists not of the Wyrm, and do more with existing ones that are like that (such as DNA). It's just too easy to kill something if it is of the Wyrm. With other kinds of antagonists, it introduces some element of moral doubt for the PCs. Presenting problems that require solutions outside of violence would be beneficial.<br /> <br /> 6) The game needs to stay away from the viewpoint that left wing politics is &quot;Gaian&quot; and if you hold right wing views, it's of the Wyrm. This was particularly prominent in the early days, but it's still been retained. It is far more pronounced than in any of the other WoD games. The game needs to take a more sober attitude and acknowledge that either political view can serve Gaia or the Wyrm. Not wanting to be lectured in a roleplay product is one reason I avoided the game for over a decade.<br /> <br /> 7) Eliminate the Beast Courts and other strange ideas the WoD had about Asian supernatural creatures being different from the rest of the world. At some point, White Wolf bit hard on multiculturalism and it didn't work out well for the game. Instead of treating other cultures respectfully, it was racist in the way only well meaning liberals can be. The Chinese have Glass Walkers, Red Talons, Shadow Lords, Silver Fangs, and other tribes just like anyone else, even if the tribal names would be translated into Chinese. I have no problem with Stargazers having high Pure Breed if they come from Tibet, but that tribe is not limited to there either. A white Stargazer is no more exceptional than an Asian Silver Fang.<br /> <br /> 8) Emphasize the differences between septs, and alliances of septs, within the Garou nation. The game almost, but not quite, captures the feeling of ancient warrior aristocracies and their feuding petty kingdoms. The game gives us conflict between the breeds and tribes, but ultimately those are too big concepts to drive major conflicts towards. Both are too large and unwieldy for politics. Septs should be the primary drivers of most politics in the game. Tribal moots and inter-Tribal concolations are rare enough that they have a limited impact, but sept politics is at a level stuff can happen. Sept alliances should be driving things in game. It would be a way to introduce some factions/sects within the Garou, but keeping the overall setting intact. Some of the tribal camps can probably be reintroduced this way. Of course, the best way to do this would be through regional sourcebooks like Rage Across the World and others.<br /> <br /> 9) <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/745840-revamping-werewolf-the-apocalypse-what-would-you-do?p=746290#post746290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dump the rather inane value disparity in the starting Rage/Gnosis/Willpower assignments.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. This is the easiest way to abuse the system in character creation so certain PCs are more powerful than others.<br /> <br /> 10) Add a bit more Totem options in the corebook. I was disappointed we didn't have ten to twelve in each category.<br /> <br /> Most of the problems that I have are with individual Tribebooks or Rage Across supplements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T10:38:33-08:00","id":747024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/745840-revamping-werewolf-the-apocalypse-what-would-you-do?p=746290#post746290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Gifts. The current Gift structure is extremely clunky. While I don't want it moved to something like Disciplines, I think there are much better ways to express their diversity that can be much easier on bookkeeping, and also help some of the weirder mechanic-to-fluff disconnects go away.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always thought that the way Gifts work is clunky. Kind of like D&amp;D spells. I'm not sure how to go about fixing them though. I think that a lot of Gifts aren't well balanced, but fixing those is different from revamping how Gifts work. Do you have any specific ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T11:50:10-08:00","id":747134,"title":"","content":"- Make most of the tribes range historically over wider territory. The Fianna and Bunyip can stay being primarily European and entirely Australian, but we've had Asian Uktena and Wendigo since first edition (Rage Across Russia), and there are other menacing wolf figures like Fenris in surprising places (like the Tiangou in China, or Rahu in India), and the obsession with triptych goddesses that the Black Furies had seems like it would fit in quite well with the Tridevi, which got imported all across Asia with the spread of Buddhism.<br /> <br /> - Name metis something else, much as how Nagah and Kitsune don't labor under having a breed named, presumably, after a Greek titaness that can so easily be mistaken for an ethnic slur. Also, remove disfigurements in favor of a flaw in keeping with the breed, like how ahi can't take defiled water.<br /> <br /> - Rename Thrall of the Wyrm so that there is actual ambiguity about where Rage comes from. Also, get rid of the correspondence between triatic Wyrms and breeds, so that there is no &quot;rape the body if you botch this roll&quot; to worry over. Note that there would still be a mechanical drawback to rolling too many successes with Rage, like not being able to stop it, but drawbacks other than that and the potential for cannibalism would be changed.<br /> <br /> - Simplify animal attraction down to adding Primal-Urge to seduction and carousing rolls.<br /> <br /> - Separate refinements to shapeshifting from Gifts, give everyone five basic forms. Eventually, you can practice and get more; these come with a minimum Primal-Urge rating coupled with an Attribute requirement, like Charms.<br /> <br /> - Level out the power of most Gifts so that they're almost entirely about spiritual ties; let none make the mistake that beginning Gifts must necessarily be equal to level one powers in other games, because seriously, Create Element is equal to several two-dot Spheres, or potentially all five dots of Lure of the Flames, <i>and that's just for one part of the Gift</i>.<br /> <br /> - Clarify how Rage goes above its normal rating, say by having each point gained after the max count for half.<br /> <br /> - Maybe have important personality facets a la Passions from Wraith, or Intimacies from Exalted 3rd edition, to help clarify how much Rage one might get from being thwarted, loss, betrayal, endangerment, etc. To further help determine when the Rage 1 Ragabash stops being so relatively calm and collected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T12:05:58-08:00","id":747145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/745840-revamping-werewolf-the-apocalypse-what-would-you-do?p=746968#post746968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 2) Too often the setting strays far away from what I think are werewolves. Instead of being based on popular culture and folklore, Garou seem to be their own fantasy race. While you can't fault players from taking things and running with it, I think those traditional elements should be emphasized in official products. In theory, the game already has concepts and mechanics to do this (Lost Cubs, Lunatics, Ronin, certain Merits and Flaws, the Curse, certain Fetishes), but in practice it does not come off that way. Instead of being prominent elements the setting has to deal with, they are things mostly ignored in my experience.<br /> <br /> 3) A major problem is overuse of Crinos form. Whenever I see some Crinos holding pistols, wearing specialized made clothing, or other things that make it &quot;normal&quot; I want to puke. It doesn't look &quot;cool&quot; to me, I think it looks lame (I may be in the minority here). It makes the Garou much more like creatures that should be in a fantasy game than in a horror game. In my game, I hold that Crinos don't have precision grip or even a true opposable thumb. People can use Homid or Glabro if they want to do that. I'd like to have the game utilize the other forms much more.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, as a forum/mush gamer of WtA, this has actually been a major selling point for me. The sept structure and the way garou work allow you to really play the game casually, even if there aren't any great events happening. You can just play everyday life of a garou, and it still will be fun and fits the setting.<br /> <br /> However, I do agree the setting does need some more traditional werewolf tropes. As I said in my post, the whole 'seeking a cure' angle is minimal. There is the whole wolf-fur wearing to become a werewolf, but not the opposite.<br /> <br /> Though, in general, I do agree about the septs. I wish there was more of a feeling of different areas ruled by different tribes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/745840-revamping-werewolf-the-apocalypse-what-would-you-do?p=746389#post746389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First I don't care for Forsaken, my personal opinion. As for setting changes:<br /> 2. Certain tribes are poorly defined and while some of have been corrected by various supplements others remain two dimensional. These tribes need a bit of an overhaul: Bone Gnawers the idea of omega wolves let alone a tribe needs to die. I have no issue with the Gnawers being misfits, or having wealth and pure breed restrictions but to have an entire tribe that actually are the largest and most likely to be ignored based on totem affiliation is problematic.<br /> 2a. The Children of Gaia need a fixed purpose and the entire privileged upper middle class whining that seems inherit to the tribe needs to die in a fire during a tornado.</div> </div> </div> </div>With Bone Gnawers, there is also the whole political aspect. One which I kinda wish was brought much more to the forefront. As well, I do dislike the whole 'Omega tribe=poverty' angle.<br /> <br /> And yup, Children of Gaia VERY MUCH need cleaning and better write ups.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T13:32:25-08:00","id":747367,"title":"","content":"No! No! No! No! Keep the Children of Gaia right where they are. They're, like, the only tribe that actually advocates <i>listening</i> to the other side, having compassion for others, and not resorting to violence as the first, second, third, last, and <i>only</i> option in <i>every</i> situation. The rest of the Garou Nation is at times frustratingly two-dimensional. The CoGs bring refreshing depth to the Garou. They're the only tribe that I even halfway like if I'm going to be putting together a PC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T13:38:57-08:00","id":747395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/745840-revamping-werewolf-the-apocalypse-what-would-you-do?p=747367#post747367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No! No! No! No! Keep the Children of Gaia right where they are. They're, like, the only tribe that actually advocates <i>listening</i> to the other side, having compassion for others, and not resorting to violence as the first, second, third, last, and <i>only</i> option in <i>every</i> situation. The rest of the Garou Nation is at times frustratingly two-dimensional. The CoGs bring refreshing depth to the Garou. They're the only tribe that I even halfway like if I'm going to be putting together a PC.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, that -isn't- at all what I'd want changed in them. It is more the cultural flavour, which is basically white middle class hippy. And the fact that too often their portrayal is all over the place in the books. The aspect you like? I'm all for it. I just wish the writers and a lot of players would be,too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T14:15:26-08:00","id":747441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/745840-revamping-werewolf-the-apocalypse-what-would-you-do?p=746372#post746372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, to 6, that is how it actually goes in the books. Galliards tell tales and renown -should- mean what is known about the character. Sadly, it isn't always done like that, and renown becomes just dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>The lore on this, and the mechanics on this, are highly disparate. That's why it's a mechanical fix, not a setting fix, in my lists. The mechanics of how Renown works makes Galliard's singing the tales of their pack a (fun for some groups) extraneous activity; rather than a fundamental aspect of the way this is handled.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for Kinfolk, their job is to be the eyes and ears of the nation among humans. They do all the jobs most garou cannot do, and report to garou any dangers they encounter. Again, it is more the way kinfolk are treated and played that creates the problem, not how they are in books. </div> </div> </div>I think this is missing my point.<br /> <br /> Why do the kinfolk want to be the eyes, and ears, of the Garou? Why do they want to do the jobs the Garou cannot? Especially since this really isn't that solid of a niche as it sounds with what the city oriented Tribes can do anyway. The books make it abundantly clear why the kinfolk are useful to the Garou, but do nothing to really sell why the Garou are useful to the kinfolk. Keeping the kinfolk around - and this is largely by the books, not something that emerges in play IME - is so heavily hanged on familial and cultural/ethnic obligation that it strains belief.<br /> <br /> The niches provided to the kinfolk only work for kinfolk that are already sold on serving the Garou against their own rational self-interest (lots of people operating in contrast to this in reality of course, so there's nothing wrong/surprising that such kin exist). Lets say your pack comes across a kin that's 25, a promising young lawyer focusing on criminal defense, with a life, a wife, and all that. How do you convince them to put that all in jeopardy for the sake of big snarling monsters they might be partially related to? Even once you get past the disbelief issues that come from someone not raised around the Garou, there's no real good pitch to make.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/745840-revamping-werewolf-the-apocalypse-what-would-you-do?p=747024#post747024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always thought that the way Gifts work is clunky. Kind of like D&amp;D spells. I'm not sure how to go about fixing them though. I think that a lot of Gifts aren't well balanced, but fixing those is different from revamping how Gifts work. Do you have any specific ideas?</div> </div> </div> </div>I do, but I'm not sure I want to clog the thread too much with this. I'll do an outline, and if people are interested I can start a different thread about it.<br /> <br /> My basic concept is somewhat like Forsaken 2e in that there's a core Gift you buy, and then you add expansions to it.<br /> <br /> The basic structure of it is the following (though an important note, if I fully develop this XP costs will be increased drastically):<br /> <br /> There are two classifications of Gifts. Birthright Gifts are the &quot;baseline&quot; Gifts of the current WtA rules of the 1-2ish Rank in power. This are Gifts that are inherently part of the Garou nature (though some splats have affinities for specific ones, though this only effects chargen and Aspects, all Brightright Gifts have the same XP cost) that the spirits help unlock from within them. Deed Gifts are rewards from the spirits for dedicated service in times of peril, or for long quests, and the like (and do not cost XP, the effort of getting them should be enough).<br /> <br /> Mechanically, all Gifts in this structure are never &quot;activated&quot; any more than an arm is activated to throw a punch and do not have level ratings. These Gifts should focus on either passive supplements to standard rolls (bonus dice, diff bonuses, expansions of normal derived things like lifting, movement distances, etc.), or the acquisition of new &quot;standard&quot; rolls for those characters (ex: Sense [Triat] becomes just an additional part of your sensory suite as natural as smell in use). Brighright Gifts focus on core fundamental powers with an eye towards utility and splat roles in the group. Deed Gifts are generally more plot/narrative focused, and should be varied slightly based on the spirit that Gifted them. For example, a Deed Gift of Prophecy from a jaggling Lune vs. one earned from Luna herself will follow the same basic rules, but the Lune's visions are likely to be more immediate in nature (which is beneficial in that it's likely to be more useful for pushing local plot forward, but limited in larger scale plots), while Luna's visions are likely to be immense in importance and be prophecies that could span generations in importance (which is beneficial for more grander scale games, and renown, but less useful if you're hoping to divine some guidance about what's going on in your Sept).<br /> <br /> Deed Gifts are a key factor in allowing Birthright Gifts (and the expansions of them to be details below) to be easier to balance mechanically, because it segregates Gifts with functions that are inherently less mechanically rigorous into a category that's immediately off the table for PCs to just buy, as well as explicitly about plot device powers.<br /> <br /> In addition to Gifts, Birthright Gifts have Aspects. Aspects are the more overt &quot;powers&quot; of the game in which your characters are clearly doing something supernatural to Gifts being more easy to disguise as &quot;just being really good&quot; at things. Aspects are also where affinities matter the most. Selecting/buying an affinity Gift nets you a free Aspect, and additional affinity aspects (if you have overlapping ones) cost less to unlock than unlocking non-affinity Aspects. This covers the intended niche protection in RAW Gifts having affinity vs. non-affinity XP costs, as well as making overlap in affinity something that isn't an overtly sub-optimal effect.<br /> <br /> Each Aspect is meant to be a distillation of the broader nature of a Gift. Homids, Glasswalkers, and Bone Gnawers might all have an Affinity for a Gift of &quot;the city&quot; or some such, but it expresses itself differently based on the Aspect. The Homid based Aspect might be more about the cultural aspects of city life, the GW Aspect about control over the city environment, and the BG Aspect about adapting to city living.<br /> <br /> All Aspects are rating 1-5. These might be a suite of powers, or one power that gets consistently stronger as thematically needed. Levels in Aspects, however, are never purchased directly. They are derived from other Traits. This means Aspects can wane in power for a Garou. It also means that starting level Garou aren't locked solely to 1-dot level powers. Most starting PCs will have at least one Aspects in the 2-3 range.<br /> <br /> Breed based Aspects grow with Rage/Gnosis/WP as the Gift thematically dictates. Breed Aspects are generally the most straight forward with more focus on &quot;this just gets better as it gets more powerful&quot; like Potence in VtM, or perhaps much more tightly controlled Spheres from MtA. These are also the ones starting PCs are going to have above a level 1 rating; as it makes sense that they've spent far more time with being human/werewolf/wolf than realizing their Auspice, or joining a Tribe.<br /> <br /> Auspice based Aspects grow with Renown (I understand some people aren't going to like this, but this presumes a change to how Renown is handled as well). This means a very wise Theurge that hasn't had major accomplishments in battle for the Glory needed for higher rank, might still have access to surprisingly potent powers. This also gives Ragabash a bit of a bonus for their harsher Renown issues, since they can choose their starting Renown; which gives them greater flexibility.<br /> <br /> Tribe based Aspects grow with Rank (making them more like the current RAW in application). This is meant to help emphasize the hierarchy inherent to Garou. A Cliath Silver Fang might be a strong leader with some oomph to back that up, but an Elder Silver Fang can issue supernaturally empowered edicts that cannot be disobeyed lightly. These are going to be more dedicated to powers-per-level style structures, and their higher levels are generally going to start to outstrip the Aspects of the other groups for it (just like Potence 5 is powerful, but doesn't really hold a candle all you can do with Dominate 5). This is a purposeful part of the balancing act. Rather than balancing just on level value alone (since they aren't purchased differently anyway) some Aspects give you more upfront but less total growth, while others are gated off until later level play, but get you better stuff for it when you get there.<br /> <br /> While I haven't entirely decided on this, mostly because the books make no attempt to be mechanically consistent with it, Camps might provide an additional Deed Gift, an additional affinity (and I need to decide, if that's the case, if this is retroactive), or an additional Aspect. I think those could be roughly equal, and it would be interesting if all Camps(/other sub-groups) had something. It also gives something for cross-Tribal camps to orient around mechanically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T15:40:14-08:00","id":747622,"title":"","content":"I am very, very leery of any setting reboot, mountain of retcons, total rewrite a-la W: the Forsaken, post-Apocalypse setting, or any other wholesale rewrite. Werewolf: the Apocalypse has warts and problems, but for the most part I love the setting as it is and I would be very sad if supplements for the game and setting I love would no longer be written.<br /> <br /> <br /> There are <b><i>minor</i></b> changes I would like to see, that I think would benefit the game if done well.<br /> <br /> 1. Clarify some things, like other posters have said, such as whether you enter breed form to sleep, or a way to make our own Totems.<br /> <br /> 2. Pure Breed is one thing I would rewrite, because as it is it doesn't make sense IMO. Does it represent your resemblance to specific ancestors, or to some hypothetical ideal? What happens to your Pure Breed if you join a tribe you weren't born to? What happens when kin or werewolves from different tribes, who both have Pure Breed, have kids together? Why do Fianna and Silent Striders have Pure Breed that makes them resemble bizarre imaginary animals instead of the actual real wolves in Europe and Africa that they supposedly breed with? If somebody born to the Red Talons joins some other tribe, or a Lupus born to another tribe joins the Red Talons, do they have the smear of red fur or not?<br /> <br /> 3. Rename the Metis. I hadn't thought of this idea before, but I would welcome it as a minor change. Otherwise don't change them, though.<br /> <br /> 4. Mechancs! I would hope that any mechanical changes would be <i><b>small</b></i> and come with a <b><i>built-in</i></b> (or free online) conversion guide for previous editions so older books don't become useless, but... there are indeed problems with the original WoD mechanics that could be fixed without a big overhaul. I would like Dexterity divorced from how fast a character can run, and the form stats for shapeshifters tweaked to reflect that more realistically. It's silly for cheetahs to have +4 Dex because they need that to run fast. Dexerity (jumping, aiming a gun, stabbing with a klaive, controlling a speeding car, crafting a fetish) should not determine how fast somebody can run. If somebody is both fast and dextrous, then those stats can reflect those traits separately. But some animals (and people) are fast and not particularly dextrous, or agile but slow.<br /> <br /> 5. Some tribes (*cough* Children of Gaia *cough*) could receive some additional material or small changes to make them more sensible, or reduce the use of dumb ethnic stereotypes or hippy dumbness. I would not want to see major changes, but small improvements and wider diversity within each tribe would be cool. I will say that Red Talons don't get to be the &quot;Wyld tribe&quot; because the Black Furies are already that. Hengeyokai could receive small changes or additions to reduce the ethnic stereotypes as well, but they already have the same Breeds and tribes as the rest of the world, they just have different names which... frankly, shapeshifters in every region of the world probably have their own translations of their names and the words for things, variant customs, and so forth. Beast Courts are mostly just politically distinct.<br /> <br /> 6. Sure, throw in some weird ronin groups that hang out with Fera or vampires or mages, or want to &quot;cure lycanthropy,&quot; or have lived in the Umbra until they turned into spirits, or have some odd philosophy that nobody else follows. Have entire camps or mini-tribes like the Siberakh and Skin-Dancers who do their own thing without joining the Garou Nation, Beast Courts, or Ahadi. Have weird rumors of mysterious groups that might be Garou, but might be something else. Have strange cults of shifters and/or kinfolk who worship weird shit in strange creepy rural towns or isolated communes. We could have a really cooky, misguided group who think that the way to save Gaia is to interbreed all the Changing-Breeds together until they &quot;merge.&quot;<br /> <br /> 7. Same with some more diversity in other Changing-Breeds -- it could be cool to have Kitsune who have spread out beyond East Asia, Mokole living in the Pacific Islands, Bagheera who join the Beast Courts, little splinters and sub-tribes of the Bastet and Ratkin and Rokea, Nagah renegades who refuse the authority of the Sesha, Ananasi who ally with other shapeshifters, etc. I don't mean entire tribes that would only make sense with large retcons of the setting history, but small or isolated groups, similar to the Siberakh.<br /> <br /> 8. Throw in some ominous prophecies and weird portents of the Apocalypse that hint at things that could happen, sort of like Rage Across the Heavens did, but instead of expanding on them and telling us where the metaplot goes, leave each as an open plot hook for STs to interpret however they want.<br /> <br /> 9. I have heard complaints from people who dislike W:tA because it depicts technology and science as evil. I can see the validity of these complaints -- as written, it kinda does. I would not want the Weaver to stop being a major antagonist, but I think there could be a subtle shift in depiction, as a force of control and stasis and smothering that <b><i>uses</i></b> science and tech a lot, instead of <b><i>being</i></b> science and tech -- much as the Wyrm abuses a lot of industrial tech but doesn't personify it. Or maybe in the way that death is technically &quot;Wyrm&quot; but is of the Balance Wyrm, not the crazy Triatic Wyrm; so science and advanced technology could be &quot;Weaver&quot; but not of the Mad Weaver. Most Garou can still be prejudiced as Hell, but the setting could move a bit away from that fear being entirely correct.<br /> <br /> 10. Positive incentives for Kinfolk to help the Garou. Sure, this is a good idea.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> There are some of things (radical changes) that I would not want to see, though:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> 1. Major setting rewrite, invalidating previous books because the setting, history, and metaplot are too different -- such as getting rid of the Hengeyokai or Black Tooth or the Wars of Rage.<br /> <br /> 2. Significant mechanics changes without easy access to a conversion guide. Any really major mechanics changes.<br /> <br /> 3. Making the tribes pan-ethnic (I think this is how it works in NWoD?)<br /> <br /> 4. Getting rid of the Striders' curse<br /> <br /> 5. Replacing W:tA's unique mythology with real-world wolfman legends. I like the current blend of taking inspiration from legends and myth, while building a mythology that's more and also distinctly different.<br /> <br /> 6. Dropping the politics. I don't want to see W:tA's discussion of real world environmental, historical, and social problems reduced to Fox News &quot;give equal time to both sides&quot; BS, or outright ignored to make it a sanitized children's game. I always liked that this game explores real world problems, the history of humans' wars against each other, and the human condition, and takes a hard look at problems in the real world that we humans need to actually fix before they kill us. That's no different from philosophical questions that Mage: the Ascension asks. That doesn't mean there has to be an objective &quot;correct&quot; question for every political controversy on the planet. Look at how the Black Furies Revised Tribebook handled abortion: different Black Furies have different opinions and some care enough to fight each other over it (because they're Garou, they just <b><i>can't</i></b> manage to get along or discuss their differences peacefully.) Nowhere does the book support any one side of the argument. Personally I'm not sure that <i><b>particular</b></i> controversy should be depicted as a big deal to the Garou, who have much bigger problems to deal with.<br /> <br /> 7. Changing how many forms each Changing-Breed has. I know that may look like a minor change to some, but it would really bug me.<br /> <br /> 8. Making a 4th edition that's post-Apocalypse. My understanding is that V:tM 4E will be post-Gehenna. I absolutely do not want to see Werewolf taken in that direction. Not at all. I am not interested in that setting except as a one-time supplement like the old Apocalypse book -- not as a definitive, one-canon-version of what happened, replacing the pre-Apocalypse books and gameline that OPP is writing currently.<br /> <br /> 9. Removing an entire Changing-Breed from the setting. I don't think any writer would do this, but I feel like mentioning it, apparently just 'cause I'm brainstorming IDK. On the other hand I <i><b>might</b></i> be alright with adding one, <i><b>if it made sense</b></i> -- I've always been confused why Kitsune are shapeshifters, but the almost identical Tanuki legends were used for Hsien instead, though my personal preference for that is to just make Tanuki a breed/tribe of Kitsune, since their animal is similar enough.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 11-01-2015, 08:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T15:47:53-08:00","id":747632,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't change a thing. I love it for what it is and the imagined differences and changes in approaches and ideal above can always be highlighted as npc or pc ideals to shake the structures of things if needed in a game without making it a part of the cWoD imo.<br /> <br /> I love it. For it warts and the bits I dont like I accept as part of setting and system and I'm ok with that. It's not real, and it doesn't have to be. It doesnt fit my personal preferences for life, but it doesnt have too for me to love it and everything that has gone into over the years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T16:12:29-08:00","id":747687,"title":"","content":"I think the one change I'd really push for is to get rid of Sense Wyrm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T16:21:14-08:00","id":747702,"title":"","content":"Honestly it sounds like a lot of the changes you lot want are what they did to forsaken.<br /> <br /> And while I love that system, I feel doing that to apocalypse would lose something in the translation. Doesn't mean I don't want it to happen though.<br /> <br /> As an aside, in the black spiral game I ran for my wife, we used the renown from the first book of the wyrm and that made level advancement stupidly easy. Hell infamy was gained daily as she had no qualms with operating in broad daylight. Burned down a vampire brothel and ate a man in a kinfolk a hotel. Better believe her name spread.<br /> <br /> Edit: the renown rules work differently in different situations I find, but almost all advancement requires some level of badassdom EXCEPT the spirals, which seems to favor intellectualism more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T16:32:40-08:00","id":747763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/745840-revamping-werewolf-the-apocalypse-what-would-you-do?p=747441#post747441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why do the kinfolk want to be the eyes, and ears, of the Garou? Why do they want to do the jobs the Garou cannot? Especially since this really isn't that solid of a niche as it sounds with what the city oriented Tribes can do anyway. The books make it abundantly clear why the kinfolk are useful to the Garou, but do nothing to really sell why the Garou are useful to the kinfolk. Keeping the kinfolk around - and this is largely by the books, not something that emerges in play IME - is so heavily hanged on familial and cultural/ethnic obligation that it strains belief.<br /> <br /> The niches provided to the kinfolk only work for kinfolk that are already sold on serving the Garou against their own rational self-interest (lots of people operating in contrast to this in reality of course, so there's nothing wrong/surprising that such kin exist). Lets say your pack comes across a kin that's 25, a promising young lawyer focusing on criminal defense, with a life, a wife, and all that. How do you convince them to put that all in jeopardy for the sake of big snarling monsters they might be partially related to? Even once you get past the disbelief issues that come from someone not raised around the Garou, there's no real good pitch to make.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vested self-interest changes in the face of the Wyrm and overbearing Weaver. If the kinfolk have even an inkling about the evil spirits and mockeries that haunt the night, they will want to have some Garou around. If you are in a warzone faced with the threat of invading enemy soldiers, it is nice to have a local garrison of friendly warriors who will help you out and certainly treat you better than the other team. Kinfolk might think they have a choice, but they don't, not really- they have to choose one side or the other, and I think that is why a lot of them serve. There are no bystanders during the Apocalypse.<br /> <br /> Saying, 'no thanks, I'd rather not' is a good way to get snatched and butchered by Pentex freaks or Black Spiral Dancers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 11-01-2015, 07:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T16:39:19-08:00","id":747781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/745840-revamping-werewolf-the-apocalypse-what-would-you-do?p=747702#post747702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly it sounds like a lot of the changes you lot want are what they did to forsaken.</div> </div> </div> </div>But... everybody who posted in this thread has different ideas. Who are you responding to?<br /> <br /> I for example mostly don't want any changes, except rather small tweaks or clarifications, or small additions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T16:39:28-08:00","id":747782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/745840-revamping-werewolf-the-apocalypse-what-would-you-do?p=747687#post747687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the one change I'd really push for is to get rid of Sense Wyrm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sense Wyrm creates a problem if you use it like Alignment, or use it exclusively to determine who the bad guys are like it is infallible.<br /> <br /> I don't do that though, and I'm very clear to my players that is the case. Whatever Sense Wyrm detects as a kind of miasma or spiritual pollution. A cancer patient in advanced stages is detected with Sense Wyrm. A physician working with medical radioactive isotope, a chemist working with mercury, the miner digging up uranium, someone just coming back from an x-ray or CAT scan, and a worker in a coal power station all show up as Wyrm tainted to a degree. In some areas, the stench is powerful enough a Garou could not distinguish anything inside it.<br /> <br /> And of course, certain Wyrm minions don't detect as well like vampires with high humanity or Fomori with certain Gifts.<br /> <br /> Sense Wyrm is just like a geiger counter that picks up things &quot;not of Gaia&quot;. But that's it. By itself it doesn't tell you much, especially in the modern day. It is just a lead you may want to follow up on. Making decisions based solely on that is a bad thing. It is a good way for STs to create hooks or leads for the PCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 11-01-2015, 08:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T17:13:00-08:00","id":747902,"title":"","content":"Really Erinys, everyone. The changes between forsaken 1st and forsaken 2nd are basically this. Hell there was a post about spirals that would basically turn them into bale hounds, which I also love. <br /> <br /> While it's done fantastic things for forsaken, I fear doing it to apocalypse as well might swing the pendulum again and make apocalypse feel like forsakens younger brother. It's gotta be delicately done, and presently the two game lines look different from each other in a refreshing way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T17:17:36-08:00","id":747909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/745840-revamping-werewolf-the-apocalypse-what-would-you-do?p=747782#post747782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sense Wyrm creates a problem is you use it like Alignment, or use it exclusively to determine who the bad guys are like it is infallible.<br /> <br /> I don't do that though, and I'm very clear to my players that is the case. Whatever Sense Wyrm detects as a kind of miasma or spiritual pollution. A cancer patient in advanced stages is detected with Sense Wyrm. A physician working with medical radioactive isotope, a chemist working with mercury, the miner digging up uranium, someone just coming back from an x-ray or CAT scan, and a worker in a coal power station all show up as Wyrm tainted to a degree. In some areas, the stench is powerful enough a Garou could not distinguish anything inside it.<br /> <br /> And of course, certain Wyrm minions don't detect as well like vampires with high humanity or Fomori with certain Gifts.<br /> <br /> Sense Wyrm is just like a geiger counter that picks up things &quot;not of Gaia&quot;. But that's it. By itself it doesn't tell you much, especially in the modern day. It is just a lead you may want to follow up on. Making decisions based solely on that is a bad thing. It is a good way for STs to create hooks or leads for the PCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then you are like the opposite of the reason why I'd want to get rid of it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Vampires aren't wyrm minions, though. They're just polluted. And they spread it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T17:19:54-08:00","id":747919,"title":"","content":"I don't think it is inherently bad to bring things over from Forsaken. If the idea works within the themes and tone of Apocalypse, why discard if because Forsaken had something similar? This new acquisition may spell the end to the NWoD in the long term. I think it would be remiss to not take any ideas that worked and add them to Apocalypse, especially if it makes it a more complete game. One of the things I see is if they want to push WtA we will need new ground so we arn't retreading the same stuff. We have over a decade of books that are still there, there will have to be a reboot and a modernizing of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T17:21:20-08:00","id":747920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/745840-revamping-werewolf-the-apocalypse-what-would-you-do?p=747909#post747909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then you are like the opposite of the reason why I'd want to get rid of it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I understood where you were coming from!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T17:24:01-08:00","id":747935,"title":"","content":"Well if 4th edition pushes last THE apocalypse like masquerade 4th, then we can look forward to a revamp. I for one would like to see a slimming of the tribes down. some will undoubtably go down into oblivion fighting the good fight (likely my beloved fenrir). The only ones I can see as a definite may well be the bone gnawers, and the spirals...<br /> <br /> We could simplify the gifts into discipline &quot;like&quot; set ups, which would be nice as well. Leave the other gifts as forgotten lore to be refound by new fledgling garou.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T19:33:02-08:00","id":748233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/745840-revamping-werewolf-the-apocalypse-what-would-you-do?p=747763#post747763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vested self-interest changes in the face of the Wyrm and overbearing Weaver. If the kinfolk have even an inkling about the evil spirits and mockeries that haunt the night, they will want to have some Garou around. If you are in a warzone faced with the threat of invading enemy soldiers, it is nice to have a local garrison of friendly warriors who will help you out and certainly treat you better than the other team. Kinfolk might think they have a choice, but they don't, not really- they have to choose one side or the other, and I think that is why a lot of them serve. There are no bystanders during the Apocalypse.<br /> <br /> Saying, 'no thanks, I'd rather not' is a good way to get snatched and butchered by Pentex freaks or Black Spiral Dancers.</div> </div> </div> </div>All of this smells too much like expecting characters to have read the books.<br /> <br /> A kin that's lived their whole life as a normal human being isn't going to be convinced the Wyrm and Weaver are out to get them because the Garou say so. If anything, the kinfolk was safer without the Garou in their lives. The kinfolk in-the-know are bigger targets than &quot;lost&quot; kinfolk. The Garou are essentially dragging kinfolk into being targets in a war that the kinfolk were previously bystanders to (whether this is true in an out-of-character sense is irrelevant). If you're 25 and having had BSDs track you down, or turned into a bane-possessed abomination... why would you believe these are significant threats? You've never seen these things before the people supposedly out to protect you came into your life. And the BSDs are perfectly willing to tell you that they're the ones that are the good guys that will save you from slavery to the Garou. Why should you believe either?<br /> <br /> The kinfolk that know they don't really have a choice were the ones raised around all this, and raised to believe being servants and breeding stock is natural. Even in the modern age though, it's pretty much impossible to have the kinfolk stay blind to how messed up the way they're treated is, if they're going to be eyes and ears out around humans.<br /> <br /> Again, from an in-character perspective, where's the motivation to accept the status quo? Why should lost kin sign up? Why should loyal kin not start protesting for change? What is the incentive?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/745840-revamping-werewolf-the-apocalypse-what-would-you-do?p=747902#post747902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really Erinys, everyone. The changes between forsaken 1st and forsaken 2nd are basically this. Hell there was a post about spirals that would basically turn them into bale hounds, which I also love.<br /> <br /> While it's done fantastic things for forsaken, I fear doing it to apocalypse as well might swing the pendulum again and make apocalypse feel like forsakens younger brother. It's gotta be delicately done, and presently the two game lines look different from each other in a refreshing way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think this is fair. Lots of us are proposing changes that are not about making things more like Forsaken in a noticeable sense. WtA has seen multiple editions, and plenty of internal changes as it is; some far more drastic than what's been suggested here.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T20:21:11-08:00","id":748281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/745840-revamping-werewolf-the-apocalypse-what-would-you-do?p=747909#post747909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then you are like the opposite of the reason why I'd want to get rid of it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Vampires aren't wyrm minions, though. They're just polluted. And they spread it.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're <u>intrinsically</u> tainted. The taint is a part of being a vampire; it doesn't leave as such at Humanity 7+, it just gets hidden.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T20:23:33-08:00","id":748286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/745840-revamping-werewolf-the-apocalypse-what-would-you-do?p=748233#post748233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All of this smells too much like expecting characters to have read the books.<br /> <br /> A kin that's lived their whole life as a normal human being isn't going to be convinced the Wyrm and Weaver are out to get them because the Garou say so. If anything, the kinfolk was safer without the Garou in their lives. The kinfolk in-the-know are bigger targets than &quot;lost&quot; kinfolk. The Garou are essentially dragging kinfolk into being targets in a war that the kinfolk were previously bystanders to (whether this is true in an out-of-character sense is irrelevant). If you're 25 and having had BSDs track you down, or turned into a bane-possessed abomination... why would you believe these are significant threats? You've never seen these things before the people supposedly out to protect you came into your life. And the BSDs are perfectly willing to tell you that they're the ones that are the good guys that will save you from slavery to the Garou. Why should you believe either?<br /> <br /> The kinfolk that know they don't really have a choice were the ones raised around all this, and raised to believe being servants and breeding stock is natural. Even in the modern age though, it's pretty much impossible to have the kinfolk stay blind to how messed up the way they're treated is, if they're going to be eyes and ears out around humans.<br /> <br /> Again, from an in-character perspective, where's the motivation to accept the status quo? Why should lost kin sign up? Why should loyal kin not start protesting for change? What is the incentive?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I don't think this is fair. Lots of us are proposing changes that are not about making things more like Forsaken in a noticeable sense. WtA has seen multiple editions, and plenty of internal changes as it is; some far more drastic than what's been suggested here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Decent points, but I don't really approach it from the same place. I don't have my werewolves relegate their families and friends, weaker though they may be, to the role of mistreated servants.<br /> What the books say and what happens to the characters in-game should not be divorced. You don't see the justification for kinfolk involvement, but I don't think it is difficult to imagine some experiences that would make the kinfolk loyal support for the Garou.<br /> <br /> In one of my games a border town near a caern came under attack by an army of renegades and mockeries. The kinfolk got a firsthand look at the horrors of the Wyrm before the Garou fought them all off. It really isn't that impossible. Another family arrived in the state fleeing Black Spiral Dancers who wanted to use them for their own ends. I don't get why you make these things sound impossible. If the kinfolk doesn't experience stuff like this, they likely won't be involved or have a good reason to fight- so I just as soon assume that it happens, sooner or later, to the kin who are featured in the story. Given the background and the methodology of the Wyrm's children, I don't think that is far fetched.<br /> <br /> Even something similar to what you mentioned, a young 20-something who has little or no experience with the Garou suddenly runs into the pack. There was a young guy, a kinfolk, who the pack had to educate, due to what would turn out to be a Mokole ancestor of his taking interest in him. The werewolves protected him from the meddling shifter, and even helped clean up his hometown.<br /> <br /> I also don't get the sense the Garou, by and large, mistreat their kin like you say they do. It isn't that the humans are captives or sex slaves; it is more akin to being family on a military base. Rules are strict, you have to follow them, you might even be in danger at some point, but the rules are for your own good and the powers that be generally care about you. The Garou are savage warriors, but most know not to direct that rage at their families, allies and friends. If the Garou aren't imperious jerks, it really isn't that hard to recruit. Not all the tribes treat their kin like the Shadow Lords.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T20:54:57-08:00","id":748320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/745840-revamping-werewolf-the-apocalypse-what-would-you-do?p=748281#post748281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They're <u>intrinsically</u> tainted. The taint is a part of being a vampire; it doesn't leave as such at Humanity 7+, it just gets hidden.</div> </div> </div> </div>This kind of talk is why I think sense wyrm should go.<br /> <br /> Not specifically because of vampires, but it is a common topic.<br /> <br /> I mean all Sense Wyrm says is that it senses Humanity 6- vampires as wyrm-tainted and Humanity 7+ as not, it doesn't say anything about intrinsic taint. Book of the Wyrm says vampires are a perversion of the natural order (true) and that they <i>often</i> bear wyrm taint.<br /> <br /> Not a complaint about Garou wanting to kill all vampires, though. That's pretty solid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 11-02-2015, 12:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T22:12:21-08:00","id":748477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/745840-revamping-werewolf-the-apocalypse-what-would-you-do?p=748320#post748320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This kind of talk is why I think sense wyrm should go.<br /> <br /> Not specifically because of vampires, but it is a common topic.<br /> <br /> I mean all Sense Wyrm says is that it senses Humanity 6- vampires as wyrm-tainted and Humanity 7+ as not, it doesn't say anything about intrinsic taint. Book of the Wyrm says vampires are a perversion of the natural order (true) and that they <i>often</i> bear wyrm taint.<br /> <br /> Not a complaint about Garou wanting to kill all vampires, though. That's pretty solid.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't about Sense Wyrm, then, because its context is &quot;useful if you're in a caern, not so much in a city&quot;. And if even you note that vampires go against the grain of the cosmos, note that there are consequences for that kind of existence, and showing up as intrinsically corrupt is perfectly reasonable. What does any given Vampire group care, anyway? No one likes vampires, even other vampires, so a fanatic hatred of vampires by something else is hardly surprising.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}